1. Array to List using Stream
    
    ```java
    Integer[] arr = {1,2,3,4};
    List<Integer> list = Arrays.stream(arr).collect(Collectors.toList());
    ```
    
2. Primitive Array to Object Array 
    
    ```java
    int[] arr = {1,2,3,4};
    Integer[] arrObj = Arrays.stream(arr).boxed().toArray(Integer[]::new);
    ```
    
3. Flatten List of List (2-D List) to List
    
    ```java
    String[][] str = new String[][]{{"a","b"}, {"c","d"}, {"c","d"}, {"e","f"}};
    
    // For List
    Arrays.stream(str).flatMap(Stream::of).collect(Collectors.toList());
    
    // For Array
    Arrays.stream(str).flatMap(Stream::of).toArray(String[]::new);
    ```
    
4. List to Map (Key as Value)
    
    ```java
    List<Integer> list = new ArrayList();
    
    Map<Integer, Integer> map = list.stream().collect(toMap(Function.identity(), Function.identity()));
    ```
    
5. List to Map (Key as Index)
    
    ```java
    List<Integer> list = new ArrayList();
    
    Map<Integer, Integer> map = list.stream().collect(toMap(list::indexof, Function.identity()));
    ```
    
6. Separate Even and ODD 
    
    ```java
